### Ruff Linting Hook
Automatically fixes lint issues when Python files are saved.

This repo uses ruff for linting and formatting (detected in `pyproject.toml` with extensive ruff configuration). Running it automatically prevents lint failures from accumulating and maintains code style consistency.

Add to `.claude/settings.json`:
```json
{
  "hooks": {
    "postToolExecution": [
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit",
        "command": "ruff check --fix \"$FILE_PATH\"",
        "description": "Auto-fix lint issues with ruff",
        "filePattern": "*.py"
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

**Setup**: `pip install ruff` (already in dev dependencies)

### MyPy Type Checking Hook
Runs type checking on modified Python files to catch type errors early.

This repo uses mypy for type checking (detected in test dependencies and confirmed by the heavy use of type hints throughout the codebase). Type safety is critical for FastAPI since the entire framework is built around type annotations.

Add to `.claude/settings.json`:
```json
{
  "hooks": {
    "postToolExecution": [
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit",
        "command": "mypy \"$FILE_PATH\"",
        "description": "Check types with mypy",
        "filePattern": "*.py"
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

**Setup**: `pip install mypy` (already in test dependencies)

### Pytest Hook for Test Files
Runs relevant tests when test files are modified to ensure changes don't break existing functionality.

This repo uses pytest extensively (detected in dependencies and `.github/workflows/test.yml`). Running tests automatically on test file changes helps catch regressions immediately.

Add to `.claude/settings.json`:
```json
{
  "hooks": {
    "postToolExecution": [
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit",
        "command": "pytest \"$FILE_PATH\" -v",
        "description": "Run modified tests",
        "filePattern": "tests/test_*.py"
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

**Setup**: `pip install pytest` (already in test dependencies)

### Large File Warning Hook
Warns when a file exceeds 500 lines, suggesting it might need refactoring.

FastAPI maintains clean, focused modules (most core files are under 300 lines). This hook helps maintain that architectural principle by flagging files that might be getting too complex.

Add to `.claude/settings.json`:
```json
{
  "hooks": {
    "postToolExecution": [
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit",
        "command": "wc -l \"$FILE_PATH\" | awk '{if($1>500) print \"⚠️  File has \" $1 \" lines - consider refactoring for maintainability\"}'",
        "description": "Warn about large files",
        "filePattern": "*.py"
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

**Setup**: Uses standard Unix tools (available on macOS/Linux, WSL on Windows)

### FastAPI Type Consistency Hook
Ensures FastAPI-specific patterns are followed, particularly around parameter functions and type annotations.

This repo has specific patterns for parameter validation (`Query()`, `Path()`, etc.) and dependency injection. This hook helps maintain consistency with FastAPI's type-driven architecture.

Add to `.claude/settings.json`:
```json
{
  "hooks": {
    "postToolExecution": [
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit",
        "command": "python -c \"import ast, sys; content=open('$FILE_PATH').read(); tree=ast.parse(content); funcs=[n for n in ast.walk(tree) if isinstance(n, ast.FunctionDef)]; routes=[f for f in funcs if any(isinstance(d, ast.Name) and d.id in ['get', 'post', 'put', 'delete', 'patch'] for d in ast.walk(f))]; print('⚠️  Route function without type hints:') if any(not f.returns for f in routes) else None\"",
        "description": "Check FastAPI route patterns",
        "filePattern": "fastapi/*.py"
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

**Setup**: Uses Python standard library (no additional dependencies)

