### ESLint Auto-Fix Hook
Automatically fixes lint issues when TypeScript/JavaScript files are saved.

This repo uses ESLint with TypeScript rules configured in `eslint.config.js`. The config includes auto-fixable rules like import ordering and unused variable removal. Running `eslint --fix` automatically prevents lint failures from accumulating.

Add to `.claude/settings.json`:
```json
{
  "hooks": {
    "postToolExecution": [
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit",
        "command": "pnpm eslint --cache --fix \"$FILE_PATH\"",
        "description": "Auto-fix ESLint issues",
        "filePattern": "\\.(ts|js|tsx|jsx)$"
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

**Setup**: ESLint is already in devDependencies with TypeScript rules configured.

### TypeScript Type Checking Hook  
Runs TypeScript compiler to catch type errors without emitting files.

The repo has comprehensive TypeScript configuration across multiple packages with strict type checking enabled. The `typecheck` script runs `tsc` across all packages to ensure type safety.

Add to `.claude/settings.json`:
```json
{
  "hooks": {
    "postToolExecution": [
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit", 
        "command": "pnpm run typecheck",
        "description": "Check TypeScript types across packages",
        "filePattern": "\\.ts$"
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

**Setup**: TypeScript is already configured in devDependencies with multiple tsconfig.json files.

### Vitest Test Runner Hook
Runs relevant unit tests when test files are modified.

This repo uses Vitest for unit testing with configuration in `vitest.config.ts`. Test files follow the `*.spec.ts` pattern in `__tests__` directories. Running tests immediately catches regressions.

Add to `.claude/settings.json`:
```json
{
  "hooks": {
    "postToolExecution": [
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit",
        "command": "pnpm run test-unit --run --reporter=basic",
        "description": "Run unit tests",
        "filePattern": "\\.spec\\.(ts|js)$"
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

**Setup**: Vitest is already in devDependencies with test configuration.

### Prettier Formatting Hook
Automatically formats code on save using Prettier.

The repo uses Prettier with configuration for consistent code formatting. The `format` script runs prettier with caching enabled. Auto-formatting prevents style inconsistencies.

Add to `.claude/settings.json`:
```json
{
  "hooks": {
    "postToolExecution": [
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit",
        "command": "pnpm prettier --write --cache \"$FILE_PATH\"",
        "description": "Format code with Prettier",
        "filePattern": "\\.(ts|js|tsx|jsx|json|md)$"
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

**Setup**: Prettier is already in devDependencies with cache configuration.

### Large File Warning Hook
Warns if a file exceeds reasonable size limits.

Vite's codebase emphasizes performance and maintainability. Large files can indicate code that should be split into smaller modules, especially important for a build tool.

Add to `.claude/settings.json`:
```json
{
  "hooks": {
    "postToolExecution": [
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit",
        "command": "wc -l \"$FILE_PATH\" | awk '{if($1>500) print \"⚠️  File has \" $1 \" lines (>500). Consider splitting into smaller modules.\"}'",
        "description": "Warn about large files"
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

**Setup**: Uses standard Unix utilities (wc, awk) available on macOS/Linux.

